From 45eef2cbeb78875930b8f554bd810000890148b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 19:57:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Document the simulation rework and index it in Reports

Records why the deconvolution simulation was rebuilt as smi_wm_60deg.m, with
the measurement behind each change rather than the rationale alone:

- the 1500-direction peak grid reported the Lmax 6 ceiling as 0.488-2.847 deg
  across orientations where sh2peaks reports 1.300 at every one, and inverted
  one arm ranking;
- the single fibre orientation was near-best for SMI and exactly worst for
  SSST-CSD, nearly doubling the apparent gap;
- a dispersed response for CSD and a delta kernel for SMI made the arms recover
  different objects, so the shared ceiling was wrong at Lmax 8;
- only SMI had a noise model, and equalising it reverses the edema comparison;
- Arm 2 minus Arm 1 measures what estimating the kernel costs: +/-0.14 deg and
  0% in fibre count, despite f being mis-estimated by 10-30%.

Also records the correction that dwi2fod csd ships -norm_lambda 1, so it does
not "only do non-negativity", and that MSMT at MRtrix defaults is
order-dependent rather than simply misconfigured.

